// near_mandate_agent.x3 — what an owner lets an AI agent spend, enforced on NEAR by x3-guard.
//
// The owner sends this once (`near_intents.py mandate args`). From then on the agent account
// can register swaps in the owner's name, and x3-guard refuses any that break a term:
//
// - `spend` and `per_payment`: Solana USDC only, at most 50 USDC a payment.
// - `per_24h`: at most 200 USDC in any rolling 24 hours (and at most 64 payments).
// - `allow recipients` / `allow assets`: where the money may go, and as what.
// - `refund_to`: a failed swap refunds here. The agent cannot point refunds at itself.
// - `require slippage` / `require fees`: the loosest bounds an agent's intent may declare.
// - `approve above`: a payment over 30 USDC waits for one of the listed approvers.
// - `expires`: the mandate ends 30 days after it is compiled. The owner can revoke it at
//   any time (`near_intents.py mandate revoke`), and every unaccepted intent stops at once.
//
// Amounts are base units: 50 USDC at six decimals is 50_000_000.
//
// The accounts are placeholders. Replace them with accounts you control.
mandate x3_shopping_agent {
    owner x3-owner.near
    agent x3-agent.near
    spend Solana.USDC
    per_payment 50000000
    per_24h 200000000
    allow recipients x3-demo.near
    allow assets Near.USDC
    refund_to 4Nd1mzi8Y1QYxJt9wZWBYZpG7S4pYkZs6YzD3Vt9aBcD
    require slippage <= 1%
    require fees <= 100 bps
    approve above 30000000 by 1 of x3-owner.near
    expires 30d
}
